Looking at this problem, I need to find the length of the crease formed when vertex A of an equilateral triangle is folded onto a point on BC.

**Setup.** Place the equilateral triangle with B = (0,0), C = (12,0), and A = (6, 6√3). The fold brings A to point P on BC with BP = 9, so P = (9, 0).

**The crease is the perpendicular bisector of segment AP**, since every point on the crease is equidistant from A and its image P.

**Midpoint of AP:** M = ((6+9)/2, (6√3+0)/2) = (15/2, 3√3).

**Direction of AP:** (3, −6√3), so the crease direction (perpendicular) is (6√3, 3) ∝ (2√3, 1).

**Parametrize the crease:** (x, y) = (15/2 + 2√3·t, 3√3 + t).

**Intersection with AB** (line y = √3·x):
3√3 + t = √3(15/2 + 2√3·t) = (15√3)/2 + 6t
⟹ 3√3 − (15√3)/2 = 5t ⟹ t = −(9√3)/10.

Point Q₁: x = 15/2 + 2√3·(−9√3/10) = 15/2 − 54/10 = 21/10, y = 3√3 − 9√3/10 = 21√3/10. ✓ (on AB, since 0 < 21/10 < 6)

**Intersection with AC** (line y = −√3·x + 12√3):
3√3 + t = −√3(15/2 + 2√3·t) + 12√3 = (9√3)/2 − 6t
⟹ 7t = (3√3)/2 ⟹ t = (3√3)/14.

Point Q₂: x = 15/2 + 2√3·(3√3/14) = 15/2 + 18/14 = 123/14, y = 3√3 + 3√3/14 = 45√3/14. ✓ (on AC, since 6 < 123/14 < 12)

**Crease length = |Q₂ − Q₁|:**

x-difference: 123/14 − 21/10 = (1230 − 294)/140 = 234/35

y-difference: √3(45/14 − 21/10) = √3·(450 − 294)/140 = 39√3/35

Distance² = (234/35)² + 3·(39/35)² = (234² + 3·39²)/35²

Computing: 234² = 54756, 39² = 1521, 3·1521 = 4563.

54756 + 4563 = 59319 = 39³ = 39·39².

So Distance = √(39·39²/35²) = **39√39 / 35**.

**Verification of form:** 39 = 3·13 (squarefree ✓), gcd(39, 35) = 1 (coprime ✓), so m = 39, n = 35, p = 39.

**m + n + p = 39 + 35 + 39 = 113**

